<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Central Bank names 20 biggest banks.</title>
<headline>Russia's Central Bank names 20 biggest banks.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a list of Russia's 20 biggest banks by assets, as provided by the Central Bank of Russia:</p>
<p>				  Assets    Authorised capital</p>
<p>				     (in trillions of roubles)</p>
<p>    Sberbank Rossii	   182.46	  19.61</p>
<p>    Vneshtorgbank RF	   24.22	   6.77</p>
<p>    Uneximbank		   20.70	   2.95</p>
<p>    Inkombank		    19.94	   1.78</p>
<p>    SBS-Agro		     13.52	   1.50</p>
<p>    Bank Menatep		 11,96	   1.06</p>
<p>    Agroprombank		 10.42	   n/a</p>
<p>    NRB			    10.20	   1.57</p>
<p>    Rossiisky Kredit	   10.11	   1.13</p>
<p>    Avtobank			9.76	   1.96</p>
<p>    IMB			     8.54	   1.22</p>
<p>    Mosbusinessbank	     8.45	   1.01</p>
<p>    Imperial			8.37	   1.53</p>
<p>    Promstroibank Rossii	7.93	   0.95</p>
<p>    IFCI			    7.73	   2.00</p>
<p>    Mezhprombank		  7.57	   1.22</p>
<p>    Tokobank			6.88	   1.17</p>
<p>    Gazprombank		   6.23	   0.85</p>
<p>    Eleksbank		     5.51	   n/a</p>
<p>    Alfa-Bank		     5.36	   n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are in trillion roubles as of May 1, 1997 and are calculated to Russian accounting standards.</p>
<p>NRB - Natsionalny Rezervny Bank, IMB - International Moscow Bank, IFCI - International Company for Finance and Investments (Mezhdunarodnaya Finansovaya Kompaniya, or MFK in Russian). ($1 = 5,760 roubles)</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
